# expect: R1003
# MEMORY-MODEL.md §1: double-free. There is no `free` to call twice in
# NOVA's real design (a region closes exactly once, at scope exit, by
# construction) -- this test exercises the explicit `close()` escape
# hatch this prototype provides specifically so double-free has a
# directly testable shape rather than being "impossible because the
# syntax doesn't exist," which would be a weaker demonstration.
region r {
    let x = alloc(r, 5);
    close(r);
    close(r);
    0
}
